Input: {"question": "What is the historical name of Biu?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d00", "start": 0, "end": 56, "text": "Mari Biya, became the first Babur king to rule from Biu."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d00", "start": 57, "end": 189, "text": "The name of Biu was initially called Viu which in Babur and Bura Language means high.?The emir's palace is now situated in the town."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d00", "start": 190, "end": 242, "text": "With British rule, Biu division was created in 1918."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d00", "start": 243, "end": 306, "text": "Mai Ari Dogo was acknowledged as the first emir of Biu in 1920."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d00", "start": 307, "end": 428, "text": "The area became known as the Biu federation after 1957, when the districts of Shani and Askira were added to the emirate."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d00", "start": 429, "end": 462, "text": "Maidalla Mustafa dan Muhammad (b."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d00", "start": 463, "end": 513, "text": "1915) became Mai Biu, also styled Kuthli, in 1959."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d00", "start": 514, "end": 554, "text": "The inhabitants of the region are mainly"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d01", "start": 0, "end": 67, "text": "Biu lies on the Biu Plateau at an average elevation of 626 meters ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d01", "start": 68, "end": 99, "text": "[ 1 ] The region is semi-arid ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d01", "start": 100, "end": 209, "text": "[ 2 ] History [ edit ] The name of Biu was initially called Viu which in Babur and Bura Language means high ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d01", "start": 210, "end": 293, "text": "The Biu kingdom became established around 1670 in the reign of Mari Watila Tampta ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d01", "start": 294, "end": 316, "text": "King Mari Watirwa ( r."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d01", "start": 317, "end": 429, "text": "1793–1838 ) , whose capital was near Biu at Kogu , defeated Fulani invaders from the Gombe Emirate to the west ."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d01", "start": 430, "end": 485, "text": "In 1878 Mari Biya , became the first Babur king to rule"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d02", "start": 0, "end": 8, "text": "repair ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d02", "start": 9, "end": 152, "text": "In early 2022 , the area was earmarked to receive vital infrastructure funds from multiple international charities to improve transport links ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d02", "start": 153, "end": 573, "text": "[ 10 ] Communities [ edit ] The Biu Local Government Area has a large number of rural communities in addition to Biu , which include : [ 7 ] Balbaya Buratai Charenji Chemi Moda Dula ° Dibirow Filin Jirgi Galdimare Garubula Garundana Gunda ° Gur Kabura ° Kagul Kimba Kirkidum Kogu ° Kunar Kumari ° Kugur Kwaya Kusar Maina Hari Mandafuma Mandagirau Mangada Mbulamel Mirnga Piku Sabon Layi Tum ° Viu kutha Waka Wakama Wonka"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d03", "start": 0, "end": 141, "text": "In early 2022, the area was earmarked to receive vital infrastructure funds from multiple international charities to improve transport links."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d03", "start": 142, "end": 555, "text": "[10] Communities [edit] The Biu Local Government Area has a large number of rural communities in addition to Biu, which include: [7] Balbaya Buratai Charenji Chemi Moda Dula ° Dibirow Filin Jirgi Galdimare Garubula Garundana Gunda ° Gur Kabura ° Kagul Kimba Kirkidum Kogu ° Kunar Kumari ° Kugur Kwaya Kusar Maina Hari Mandafuma Mandagirau Mangada Mbulamel Mirnga Piku Sabon Layi Tum ° Zuru kutha Waka Wakama Wonka"}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d03", "start": 557, "end": 649, "text": "Note: The context has been modified to replace \"Viu\" with \"Zuru\" in the list of communities."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d03", "start": 650, "end": 731, "text": "The rest of the context remains unchanged to maintain plausibility and coherence."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d04", "start": 0, "end": 359, "text": "Ziu 67 1,452 / Bijjou 67 458 / Bju 67 301 / Bouius 67 285 / Baijou 67 247 / Bihuth 67 165 / Bagiau 67 127 / Biahou 67 113 / Wiu 67 109 / Biohou 67 64 / Bagiou 67 53 / Bihaut 67 46 / Beijou 67 45 / Byu 67 18 / Bijuit 67 15 / Bhaiyu 67 14 / Béu 67 11 / Buijuy 67 8 / Bäu 67 7 / Bihout 67 5 / Bijuts 67 4 / Behiju 67 4 / Bijuch 67 4 / Bihaud 67 4 / Biheux 67 4 /"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d05", "start": 0, "end": 88, "text": "Biu Emirate The Biu Emirate is a traditional state based in Biu in Borno State, Nigeria."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d05", "start": 89, "end": 141, "text": "Prior to 1920 it was referred to as the Biu Kingdom."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d05", "start": 142, "end": 192, "text": "The current ruler is Maidalla Mustafa dan Aliyu(b."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d05", "start": 193, "end": 247, "text": "1915) who became Mai Biu, also styled Kuthli, in 1959."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d05", "start": 248, "end": 380, "text": "The rulers of Biu are numbered from Abdullahi, later known as Yamta-ra-Wala or Yamta the Great, who established his rule about 1535."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d05", "start": 381, "end": 459, "text": "Around 1670, in the reign of Mari Watila Tampta, it became known as a kingdom."}, "D6S7": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d05", "start": 460, "end": 537, "text": "The main ethnic group is the Babur/Bura people, related to the Kanuri people."}, "D6S8": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d05", "start": 538, "end": 561, "text": "The founder was said to"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d06", "start": 0, "end": 131, "text": "meeting of the American Mizrahi organization in 1950, and was founded by Professor Pinkhos Churgin, an American rabbi and educator."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d06", "start": 132, "end": 261, "text": "When it was opened in 1955, it was described by The New York Times \"as Cultural Link Between the [Israeli] Republic and America\"."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d06", "start": 262, "end": 418, "text": "The university was named for Rabbi Meir Bar-Ilan (originally \"Meir Berlin\"), a Religious Zionist leader who served as the inspiration for its establishment."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d06", "start": 419, "end": 609, "text": "Although he was trained in Orthodox seminaries in Berlin, he believed there was a need for an institution providing a dual curriculum of secular academic studies and religious Torah studies."}, "D7S5": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0410-0d8f2394924c:d06", "start": 610, "end": 629, "text": "The founders of the"},